category: Security
requires: cygwin libxml2 libxmlsec1_1
sdesc: "One-time password components (pskc runtime)"
ldesc: "OATH Toolkit provide components to build one-time password authentication systems. It contains shared C libraries, command line tools and a PAM module. Supported technologies include the event-based HOTP algorithm (RFC 4226), the time-based TOTP algorithm (RFC 6238), and Portable Symmetric Key Container (PSKC, RFC 6030) to manage secret key data. OATH stands for Open AuTHentication, which is the organization that specify the algorithms."
external-source: oath-toolkit

